This is the Rust/LLVM dual-licensing arrangement: the MIT option keeps
things simple, the Apache option adds an explicit patent grant, and the
LLVM exception removes the attribution requirement for the runtime
that AHC-compiled programs link against — so a binary produced by
`ahc build` carries no notice obligation from the compiler itself.

Unless you explicitly state otherwise, any contribution intentionally
submitted for inclusion in this work by you shall be dual-licensed as
above, without any additional terms or conditions.
